      "message": "This also changes the project-level diff API’s behavior for nonexistent files: previously 404, now 200 with an empty diff. I added tests in change 647243 capturing the existing behaviour. They pass before this change and fail afterward.\n\nThe change-level diff API already intentionally returns an empty diff, as covered by RevisionDiffIT.diffOfNonExistentFileIsAnEmptyDiffResult().\n\nIs aligning those behaviors intentional? If so, could we explicitly test the new project-level behaviour (and adapt my new tests)? Otherwise, could we preserve 404 when the path exists in neither commit?\n\nIf preserving the existing project-level 404 behavior is preferred, one possible implementation is to add this in GetDiffFile.apply(), after verifyPathVisibility(...):\n\n```java\nif (!Patch.isMagic(filePath)) {\n  try (TreeWalk baseFile \u003d TreeWalk.forPath(repo, filePath, baseCommit.getTree());\n      TreeWalk newFile \u003d TreeWalk.forPath(repo, filePath, newCommit.getTree())) {\n    if (baseFile \u003d\u003d null \u0026\u0026 newFile \u003d\u003d null) {\n      throw new ResourceNotFoundException(filePath);\n    }\n  }\n}\n```",
